This pattern is only consulted via `resolveYamlFloat$1(source, isExplicit)` when `isExplicit === true`, i.e. when a scalar carries an explicit tag like `!!float` and is constructed through `constructScalar` under `JSON_SCHEMA` (the only schema containing `floatJsonTag`; the default `CORE_SCHEMA` uses `floatCoreTag` and `DUMP_SCHEMA` uses `floatYaml11Tag`/`floatCoreTag`, so only JSON_SCHEMA is affected).

Before the patch, `!!float 1e5` matched the explicit pattern (optional sign), parsed to `100000`, and returned a number. After the patch, `1e5` fails the first alternative (no sign after `e`) and doesn't match the second alternative (which requires a leading `.` and still has an optional sign — so the pattern is now internally inconsistent with its own second alternative and with the unchanged implicit pattern), so `resolve` returns `NOT_RESOLVED` and the loader throws `cannot resolve a node with !<tag:yaml.org,2002:float> explicit tag`. This is an observable regression: implicit `1e5` under JSON_SCHEMA still resolves (implicit pattern untouched), but the explicit form now throws where it previously worked.

